{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528210-rage-across-vancouver","id":1528210,"title":"Rage Across Vancouver","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-08T07:42:54-08:00","id":1528210,"title":"Rage Across Vancouver","content":"<a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/466644/Rage-Across-Vancouver-Island\" target=\"_blank\">Rage across Vancouver Island</a> is a setting book made by WtA friends of mine of their long-term setting.<br /> <br /> Here is their desc of the book;<br /> <br /> <i>Off the coast of British Columbia lies one of the last bastions of Gaia. Covered in thick, old-growth boreal rainforests, Vancouver Island is as unique as it is fragile. Even here, the Wyrm and its armies of smog-choked machines seek to clear-cut the ancient forests and leave tar and barren earth in their place. Here, among cedars and firs hundreds of years old or more, the Garou and their Fera cousins must set aside the scars of the War of Rage to better protect their home and way of life.<br /> <br /> Rage Across Vancouver Island takes a look at an area of the world that the official World of Darkness material has never covered in detail. It covers the unique culture among the Changing Breeds that\u2019s evolved over thousands of years of isolation, including the strange offshoots of the Garou and Fera that have cropped up there. It covers the local spirit-scape of the Island, and the caerns that have been opened across it over the course of its history. It also details the predation of the Wyrm on such a fragile ecosystem, featuring a nefarious Pentex subsidiary dedicated to logging and lumber</i><br /> <br /> Having played in this setting, I highly recommend it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" targe